startRace (game.ts:271-299) is synchronous: createWorld, sceneFor() -> createRaceScene (all track-chunk and prop-cell meshes with hull/crease, new materials; old scene disposed when track or car count changed), scene.resize, ui.reset, draw(race,1,0) -> scene.render() (the first WebGL draw of the session when RACE is pressed from the menu). The CSS wipe (animation: ui-screen-sweep var(--duration-wipe)) only starts at the first frame rendered after the click handler returns.
Trace: t=0 tap RACE -> timer due at t=330; startRace blocks D ms; first paint of the overlay (animation t=0) at >=D; element.remove() fires at max(330, D). D=200 ms: band on screen for 130 of its 250 ms sweep and removed while the navy cover still hides the screen (it clears the right edge about 155-165 ms in), so the race pops in mid-sweep. D>=330 ms: removed before it is painted (or one navy frame). RETRY on the same track only calls scene.reset() and is cheap.
Repro (Vitest, fake timers): mock createRaceScene as () => { vi.advanceTimersByTime(300); return {update(){},render(){},reset(){},resize(){},dispose(){}}; }, click RACE, then vi.advanceTimersByTime(30): [data-screen-change="chequer"] is already gone, 30 ms after the race became visible. Expected: still on show for at least 250 ms after startRace returns.
